    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262">

                <pb facs="0900" n="865" sameAs="frus:frus1977-80v09Ed2/pg865"/>

                <head>262. Memorandum From the President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs
                    (Brzezinski) to Secretary of State Vance and Secretary of Defense Brown<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d262-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1979-06-12">June 12, 1979</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Military Assistance for Egypt (S)</item>
                </list>
                <p>In the light of yesterday’s discussions with Vice President Mubarak,<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d262-f2"/> it would be useful to have a prompt review<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d262-f3"/> of the practicalities <pb facs="0901" n="866"
                        xml:id="pg866"/> of enhanced U.S. military assistance to Egypt, perhaps
                    stretched out over a somewhat longer period of time. The President would like to
                    have the above by the time of his return from Vienna.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d262-f4"/> (S)</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#bold">Zbigniew Brzezinski</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
